## [upstream] min: fix the parabolic-step test in the Brent minimiser

Commit: c27559ec6

`brent_iterate()` takes the parabolic step `p/q` only when the trial point
`u = z + p/q` lies inside the bracket.  With `q` made positive that is
`-q*w_lower < p < q*w_upper`, but the code tested `p < q*w_lower`, which
admits trial points below `x_left` and rejects many valid parabolic steps,
forcing golden-section steps.  A transcription error from Brent's Algol 60;
netlib `fmin`, Numerical Recipes, Forsythe et al. and Boost all have the
corrected form.

Files: `min/brent.c`, plus a regression test in `min/test.c`/`min/test_funcs.c`.

See Savannah bug #43496.


