## [rejected] integration: qagiu on cosh(x) exp(-cosh(x))

Not a library bug; no change.  Savannah bug #59911 asks why
`gsl_integration_qagiu()` fails on

    int_0^inf cosh(x) exp(-cosh(x)) dx

with "bad integrand behavior".  The `qagiu` transformation evaluates
the integrand at `x = (1 - t)/t`, which grows without bound as
`t -> 0`.  For `x > ~710.5`, `cosh(x)` overflows to `+Inf`,
`exp(-cosh(x))` underflows to 0, and the product is `NaN`; that NaN
reaches the quadrature.  With a 1000-interval workspace the call
