`GAMMA_INC_A_0(x, result)` is a one-line alias for
`gsl_sf_expint_E1_e(x, result)` used in two places.  Removing it adds no
correctness; it is a pure readability refactor, outside the eligibility
rule for this review.  Not a bug.

### #68704 - introduce gsl_histogram_variance

A feature request for a new public function `gsl_histogram_variance`,
proposing that `gsl_histogram_sigma` be renamed and a square-rooting
wrapper kept for compatibility.  New API, and the proposed rename breaks
the existing name; `histogram/stat.c` is numerically correct as it
