## [upstream] integration: Gauss-Lobatto, Gauss-Radau, Clenshaw-Curtis and Fejer rules

Commit: 7cdd25747 (documentation: 4ad7f6f36)

Savannah bug #32257 (2011) points at the LGPL `quadrule` collection and
suggests importing, in particular, Lobatto quadrature.  Four rules were
added to the `gsl_integration_fixed` framework:

    gsl_integration_fixed_lobatto          (exact to degree 2n-3)
    gsl_integration_fixed_radau            (exact to degree 2n-2)
    gsl_integration_fixed_clenshaw_curtis  (exact to degree n-1)
    gsl_integration_fixed_fejer            (exact to degree n-1)

Radau uses the standard Jacobi-matrix path with the last diagonal
element set to `n/(2n-1)`, which places the right endpoint on the node
set.  Lobatto, Clenshaw-Curtis and Fejer are not Gaussian quadratures of
a positive weight, so the public `gsl_integration_fixed_type` gained an
optional `nodes` callback that fills the nodes and weights directly;
existing types leave it null and keep the previous behaviour.  The
Lobatto interior nodes are the roots of `P'_{n-1}` (computed as the
eigenvalues of the Jacobi(1,1) matrix) with weights
`2/(n(n-1) P_{n-1}(x_i)^2)`, and the Clenshaw-Curtis and Fejer weights
come from their closed-form cosine series.

Verification: the four rules integrate a degree-5 monomial exactly on
several intervals (including a reversed one) and `exp(x)` to the
accuracy implied by their exactness degree; the weight formulas were
checked against the mpmath moment equations.  Negative control:
flipping the sign of the Fejer cosine series fails the new checks, while
the restored tree is clean.  Full ctest 56/56 on MSVC x64.

Files: `integration/lobatto.c`, `radau.c`, `clenshaw_curtis.c`,
`fejer.c`, `integration/gsl_integration.h`, `integration/fixed.c`,
`integration/Makefile.am`, `cmake/gsl_sources.cmake`,
`integration/test.c`, both manuals.

See Savannah bug #32257.










